87</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Reeves</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A randomised controlled trial to assess the effectiveness and cost of a patient orientated self management approach to chronic inflammatory bowel disease</article-title><source>Gut</source><year>2004</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>1639</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15479685</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thoolen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>De Ridder</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bensing</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The effectiveness of a self-management intervention in patients with screen-detected type-2 diabetes</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2007</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>2832</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17666461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Norris</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Engelgau</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Narayan</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effectiveness of self management training in type 2 diabetes: a systematic review of randomized controlled trials</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>561</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11289485</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Griffin</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinmonth</surname><given-names>A-L</given-names></name><name><surname>Veltman</surname><given-names>MWM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillard</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Grant</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect on health-related outcomes of interventions to alter the interaction between patients and practitioners: a systematic review of trials</article-title><source>Ann Fam Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>608</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15576546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="web"><collab>Australian Department of Health and Ageing</collab><source>45 Year old Health Check</source><year>2006</year><access-date>accessed August 2007</access-date><comment>MBS item 717 <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.health.gov.au/internet/wcms/publishing.nsf/Content/health-epc-45check">http://www.health.gov.au/internet/wcms/publishing.nsf/Content/health-epc-45check</ext-link></comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>